  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nDespite a lengthy period of dry weather, rain chances make a \nsubstantial jump on Saturday thanks to weakening Isaias moving \nnorth from the Gulf Coast. This tropical system will bring \nabundant moisture to the area along with forcing for ascent as it \nmerges with an upper-level disturbance moving northeast from the \nArkLaTex region. Widespread rain chances are in the forecast for \nMiddle Tennessee Saturday into Sunday, and heaviest rainfall is \nforecast on Saturday. Overall rain amounts of 1-3\" are expected. \nThis will be a beneficial rain event to our area experiencing \ndrought. At this time we're not expecting any significant impacts \nto Middle Tennessee, though we'll be monitoring forecast details \nclosely, especially those associated with thunderstorm potential. \nGusty winds of 30-40 mph remain possible on Saturday.\n\nOnce the remnants of Isaias depart to the northeast on Monday,\nwe'll return back to more stable, dry weather with warm afternoons\nand cool nights that remain in the forecast into mid next week.",
